ganizers of transmembrane signals</article-title><source>Cell.</source><volume>80</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>257</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7834744</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Parketal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Raman</surname><given-names>K.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>K.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferran</surname><given-names>L.J.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chow</surname><given-names>W.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stern</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>A.M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Suppression of accelerated diabetic atherosclerosis by the soluble receptor for advanced glycation endproducts</article-title><source>Nat. Med.</source><volume>4</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>1025</fpage><lpage>1031</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9734395</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Parkkinenetal1993"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parkkinen</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Raulo</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Merenmies</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nolo</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kajander</surname><given-names>E.O.</given-names></name><name><surname>Baumann</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rauvala</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Amphoterin, the 30 kDa protein in a family of HMG1-type polypeptides</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><volume>268</volume><year>1993</year><fpage>19726</fpage><lpage>19738</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8366113</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ParkkinenandRauvala1991"><citation cita